<title>SOUTH KOREA: Strikes cost S.Korea 2.12 trln won in lost output.</title>
<headline>Strikes cost S.Korea 2.12 trln won in lost output.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea is expected to post 2.12 trillion won in lost production by the end of Tuesday due to nationwide labour strikes, a trade ministry official said.</p>
<p>Lost exports from the industrial action that started on December 26 were estimated at $393 million, he said.  </p>
<p>South Korea's major industries have been hit by strikes called to protest at a new labour law rammed through parliament by the ruling party.</p>
<p>The law allows employers to lay off workers, replace strikers and implement flexible work hours.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5644</p>
</text>
